\par\intbl \cf1 Born among the Madagascar brain mines, she toiled in a thought-shop for years, plugged into a human-powered computer network leased to the Ugandan military. With few social skills, Persis excelled at solitary operations when she joined the resistance effort. When the Cybrids swept through North Africa, Persis was one of the advance scouts who provided reconnaissance on the Niger River line,  while the first tunnels of Sub-Congo were drilled.
