\trowd\trgaph105\trleft84 \cellx8005\cellx8275\cellx8545\cellx8815\cellx9085\cellx9355\pard\intbl\qc\tx1705\tx2695\tx3955\tx5395\tx6925 \pard\intbl\tx1705\tx2695\tx3955\tx5395\tx6925 \par\pard \pard\intbl Jarvis learned to fight in the tunnels of New Chicago late in the first Cybrid conflicts. A street tough, his future seemed short and grim. Then he stumbled on a computer record of a distant ancestor who fought heroically in Earth\'92s first World War. He identified the picture of his ancestor, standing proudly in uniform, and this discovery changed his life. He decided there was no honor dying in the streets, and if he had to die, he would die a warrior. He placed a copy of the picture in a gold locket which he kept with him the rest of his life, a good-luck charm, and volunteered as a Herc pilot.  Intelligent, possessed of well-rounded abilities, Jarvis became an excellent warrior. He entered the conflict too late to see much action, but he was twice decorated, and remained a career military man until his retirement. He died in bed at his family home in New Chicago.
